+// countBound is how many lines the count holds. Every frame is still counted: once the bound is
+// reached, a frame of a new destination goes to its kind's "other destinations" line. Without a
+// bound, main decides how much of the Mac's memory and disk the count takes (a scan of 10.0.0.0/8
+// is 16.7 million lines, rewritten twice a second).
+const countBound = 256
